{
  "title": "Effect of Rising Demand on Price",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Set Up the Market Axes",
      "say": "Let's begin by drawing the market axes, with price on the vertical axis and quantity on the horizontal axis.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "main_title", "x": 80, "y": 50, "text": "What Happens to Price When Demand Rises?", "size": 52 },
        { "op": "line", "id": "axis_p", "x1": 220, "y1": 720, "x2": 220, "y2": 190, "arrow": true, "width": 5 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_p", "x": 130, "y": 180, "text": "Price (P)", "size": 32 },
        { "op": "line", "id": "axis_q", "x1": 220, "y1": 720, "x2": 880, "y2": 720, "arrow": true, "width": 5 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_q", "x": 890, "y": 705, "text": "Quantity (Q)", "size": 32 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Initial Supply and Demand Curves",
      "say": "The upward-sloping supply curve shows sellers offer more at higher prices, while the downward-sloping demand curve reflects buyers' willingness to pay.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "line", "id": "curve_s", "x1": 300, "y1": 660, "x2": 760, "y2": 280, "color": "gray", "width": 5 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_s", "x": 775, "y": 265, "text": "Supply (S)", "size": 34, "color": "gray" },
        { "op": "line", "id": "curve_d1", "x1": 300, "y1": 320, "x2": 700, "y2": 680, "color": "ink", "width": 5 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_d1", "x": 715, "y": 675, "text": "Demand (D₁)", "size": 34, "color": "ink" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Initial Equilibrium",
      "say": "Where supply and demand intersect at E₁, the market determines the initial equilibrium price P₁ and quantity Q₁.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "ellipse", "id": "dot_e1", "cx": 500, "cy": 500, "rx": 7, "ry": 7, "fill": "ink" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_e1", "x": 515, "y": 480, "text": "E₁", "size": 30 },
        { "op": "line", "id": "dash_p1", "x1": 500, "y1": 500, "x2": 220, "y2": 500, "color": "gray", "dash": true, "width": 3 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_p1", "x": 165, "y": 485, "text": "P₁", "size": 32 },
        { "op": "line", "id": "dash_q1", "x1": 500, "y1": 500, "x2": 500, "y2": 720, "color": "gray", "dash": true, "width": 3 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_q1", "x": 485, "y": 735, "text": "Q₁", "size": 32 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Demand Increases and Shifts Right",
      "say": "When demand rises, consumers want to purchase more at every price level, shifting the entire demand curve outward to D₂.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "line", "id": "curve_d2", "x1": 420, "y1": 320, "x2": 820, "y2": 680, "color": "blue", "width": 5 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_d2", "x": 835, "y": 675, "text": "Demand (D₂)", "size": 34, "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "line", "id": "arrow_shift", "x1": 540, "y1": 420, "x2": 630, "y2": 420, "color": "blue", "arrow": true, "width": 4 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "txt_shift", "x": 535, "y": 380, "text": "Demand Rises", "size": 28, "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "New Equilibrium Forms",
      "say": "At the original price P₁, an immediate shortage occurs. Eager buyers compete and bid prices upward until reaching equilibrium E₂.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "ellipse", "id": "dot_e2", "cx": 560, "cy": 445, "rx": 7, "ry": 7, "fill": "blue", "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_e2", "x": 575, "y": 425, "text": "E₂", "size": 30, "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "line", "id": "dash_p2", "x1": 560, "y1": 445, "x2": 220, "y2": 445, "color": "blue", "dash": true, "width": 3 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_p2", "x": 165, "y": 430, "text": "P₂", "size": 32, "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "line", "id": "dash_q2", "x1": 560, "y1": 445, "x2": 560, "y2": 720, "color": "blue", "dash": true, "width": 3 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl_q2", "x": 545, "y": 735, "text": "Q₂", "size": 32, "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "line", "id": "arrow_p_up", "x1": 150, "y1": 490, "x2": 150, "y2": 445, "color": "red", "arrow": true, "width": 4 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "say": "In conclusion, an increase in demand creates upward pressure on price, resulting in both a higher price and a greater quantity sold.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "rect", "id": "panel_sum", "x": 980, "y": 210, "w": 540, "h": 440, "color": "ink", "width": 3, "fill": "gray" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "txt_sum_title", "x": 1020, "y": 250, "text": "Mechanism & Outcome", "size": 38, "underline": true },
        { "op": "write", "id": "txt_step1", "x": 1020, "y": 315, "text": "1. Buyers demand more (D₁ → D₂)", "size": 32 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "txt_step2", "x": 1020, "y": 370, "text": "2. Shortage at old price P₁", "size": 32 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "txt_step3", "x": 1020, "y": 425, "text": "3. Competition bids price up", "size": 32 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "txt_final", "x": 1020, "y": 505, "text": "Result:\n• Price RISES (P₁ → P₂)\n• Quantity RISES (Q₁ → Q₂)", "size": 36, "color": "red" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Why Does the Pythagorean Theorem Work?",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "The Claim",
      "say": "For any right triangle, does a² + b² really always equal c²? Let's prove it visually with an elegant area puzzle.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "t-main", "x": 800, "y": 50, "text": "Why Does the Pythagorean Theorem Work?", "size": 52, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "t-sub", "x": 800, "y": 115, "text": "A Visual Proof by Area Rearrangement", "size": 30, "color": "gray", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "path", "id": "intro-tri", "d": "M 240 460 L 480 460 L 480 340 Z", "color": "ink", "width": 4, "fill": "gray" },
        { "op": "path", "id": "intro-sq", "d": "M 460 460 L 460 440 L 480 440", "color": "ink", "width": 3 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "intro-lbl-b", "x": 360, "y": 475, "text": "b", "size": 32, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "intro-lbl-a", "x": 505, "y": 395, "text": "a", "size": 32, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "intro-lbl-c", "x": 340, "y": 380, "text": "c", "size": 32, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "intro-claim", "x": 750, "y": 380, "text": "Target: Prove that  a² + b² = c²", "size": 42, "color": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Build the Big Square",
      "say": "We construct a large square with side length a + b, and place four copies of our right triangle along its corners.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "erase", "ids": ["intro-tri", "intro-sq", "intro-lbl-a", "intro-lbl-b", "intro-lbl-c", "intro-claim"] },
        { "op": "rect", "id": "outer-sq", "x": 200, "y": 240, "w": 360, "h": 360, "color": "ink", "width": 4 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-top-a", "x": 260, "y": 200, "text": "a", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-top-b", "x": 440, "y": 200, "text": "b", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-right-a", "x": 580, "y": 295, "text": "a", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-right-b", "x": 580, "y": 490, "text": "b", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-bot-b", "x": 320, "y": 615, "text": "b", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-bot-a", "x": 500, "y": 615, "text": "a", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-left-b", "x": 170, "y": 350, "text": "b", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-left-a", "x": 170, "y": 535, "text": "a", "size": 28, "color": "ink", "anchor": "middle" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Inner Square",
      "say": "Connecting the vertices forms an inner square tilted inside, with each edge equal to hypotenuse c.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "path", "id": "inner-sq", "d": "M 320 240 L 560 360 L 440 600 L 200 480 Z", "color": "blue", "width": 4, "fill": "blue" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-c1", "x": 245, "y": 345, "text": "c", "size": 30, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-c2", "x": 450, "y": 285, "text": "c", "size": 30, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-c3", "x": 515, "y": 490, "text": "c", "size": 30, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-c4", "x": 310, "y": 550, "text": "c", "size": 30, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-c-area", "x": 380, "y": 405, "text": "c²", "size": 44, "color": "blue", "anchor": "middle" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lbl-tri-tag", "x": 240, "y": 270, "text": "½ab", "size": 24, "color": "gray" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Method 1: Sum of the Parts",
      "say": "The total area can be written as the area of the 4 outer triangles plus the inner square c².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "m1-title", "x": 760, "y": 240, "text": "Method 1: Pieces of the Square", "size": 34, "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "m1-line1", "x": 760, "y": 290, "text": "Total Area = 4 × (Triangle) + Center Square", "size": 30, "color": "ink" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "m1-line2", "x": 760, "y": 335, "text": "           = 4 × (½ · a · b) + c²", "size": 30, "color": "ink" },
