{
  "title": "Why a² + b² = c² works",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "The claim",
      "say": "For any right triangle with legs a and b and hypotenuse c, the squares on the legs add up to the square on the hypotenuse. We will prove it by comparing areas.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "title", "x": 100, "y": 70, "text": "Why a² + b² = c² works", "size": 56 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "claim", "x": 100, "y": 130, "text": "Claim: legs a, b and hypotenuse c", "size": 32, "color": "gray" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Build a big square",
      "say": "Place four copies of the same right triangle inside a square whose side is a + b. The square's area is (a + b)².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "rect", "id": "big", "x": 100, "y": 180, "w": 400, "h": 400, "color": "ink", "width": 5 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lblA", "x": 180, "y": 140, "text": "a", "size": 32, "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lblB", "x": 50, "y": 300, "text": "b", "size": 32, "color": "blue" },
        { "op": "write", "id": "lblSide", "x": 300, "y": 130, "text": "side = a + b", "size": 32 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Four triangles",
      "say": "Each corner holds a right triangle with legs a and b. Together they cover four triangles, each with area ab/2.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "path", "id": "t1", "d": "M100 180 L260 180 L100 420 Z", "color": "blue", "width": 4, "fill": "blue" },
        { "op": "path", "id": "t2", "d": "M500 180 L260 180 L500 340 Z", "color": "blue", "width": 4, "fill": "blue" },
        { "op": "path", "id": "t3", "d": "M500 580 L340 580 L500 340 Z", "color": "blue", "width": 4, "fill": "blue" },
        { "op": "path", "id": "t4", "d": "M100 580 L340 580 L100 420 Z", "color": "blue", "width": 4, "fill": "blue" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The tilted square",
      "say": "The four hypotenuses enclose a tilted square. Its side is c, so its area is c².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "path", "id": "inner", "d": "M260 180 L500 340 L340 580 L100 420 Z", "color": "red", "width": 6 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "c2", "x": 300, "y": 380, "text": "c²", "size": 44, "color": "red", "anchor": "middle" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Compare the areas",
      "say": "The big square equals the four triangles plus the tilted square. Write that as an equation.",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "eq1", "x": 700, "y": 220, "text": "Big square = (a + b)²", "size": 40 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "eq2", "x": 700, "y": 290, "text": "= 4 triangles + c²", "size": 40 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "eq3", "x": 700, "y": 360, "text": "= 4 · (ab/2) + c²", "size": 40 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Algebra",
      "say": "Expand the left side and simplify. The 2ab terms cancel, leaving a² + b² = c².",
      "ops": [
        { "op": "write", "id": "alg1", "x": 700, "y": 460, "text": "a² + 2ab + b² = 2ab + c²", "size": 40 },
        { "op": "write", "id": "alg2", "x": 700, "y": 540, "text": "a² + b² = c²", "size": 52, "color": "green", "underline": true }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Why it always holds",
