{
  "title": "Why Pythagoras Works",
  "lang": "en",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "The claim",
      "say": "In a right triangle with legs a and b and hypotenuse c, the squares on the legs add up to the square on the hypotenuse.",
      "ops": [
        {"id":"t1","op":"write","x":800,"y":50,"text":"Why Pythagoras Works","size":56,"anchor":"middle","color":"blue"},
        {"id":"tri1","op":"path","d":"M 250 650 L 250 350 L 650 650 Z","width":5},
        {"id":"la","op":"write","x":190,"y":480,"text":"a","size":36},
        {"id":"lb","op":"write","x":440,"y":670,"text":"b","size":36},
        {"id":"lc","op":"write","x":480,"y":440,"text":"c","size":36},
        {"id":"f1","op":"write","x":1100,"y":450,"text":"a² + b² = c²","size":52,"anchor":"middle","color":"red"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Build a big square",
      "say": "Take four copies of the triangle and arrange them inside a square whose side is a plus b.",
      "ops": [
        {"id":"e1","op":"erase","ids":["tri1","la","lb","lc","f1"]},
        {"id":"big","op":"rect","x":300,"y":200,"w":500,"h":500,"width":5},
        {"id":"sidetop","op":"write","x":550,"y":140,"text":"a + b","size":34,"anchor":"middle","color":"gray"},
        {"id":"sideleft","op":"write","x":170,"y":430,"text":"a + b","size":34,"color":"gray"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tilted square inside",
      "say": "Place the four triangles in the corners. Their hypotenuses form a tilted square in the middle, with side c.",
      "ops": [
        {"id":"q1","op":"line","x1":380,"y1":200,"x2":800,"y2":280,"color":"blue","width":5},
        {"id":"q2","op":"line","x1":800,"y1":280,"x2":720,"y2":700,"color":"blue","width":5},
        {"id":"q3","op":"line","x1":720,"y1":700,"x2":300,"y2":620,"color":"blue","width":5},
        {"id":"q4","op":"line","x1":300,"y1":620,"x2":380,"y2":200,"color":"blue","width":5},
        {"id":"cl","op":"write","x":550,"y":420,"text":"c²","size":48,"anchor":"middle","color":"red"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Count the area: way one",
      "say": "The big square's area equals the tilted square plus four triangles, each with area one half a times b.",
      "ops": [
        {"id":"w1","op":"write","x":900,"y":250,"text":"Big square =\n c² + 4 · ½ab\n = c² + 2ab","size":42}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Count the area: way two",
      "say": "But the big square has side a plus b, so its area is a plus b, squared, which expands to a squared plus 2ab plus b squared.",
      "ops": [
        {"id":"w2","op":"write","x":900,"y":520,"text":"Big square =\n (a + b)²\n = a² + 2ab + b²","size":42}
      ]
